    "result_text": "All 264 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS** (Failures: 0, Errors: 0). The `ERROR`/stack-trace log lines are expected error-path logging from tests exercising failure handling, not test failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Replaced the `customer_code` and `membership_number` columns/fields (and their accessors) with a single `member_id` / `memberId`.\n\n- **DB schemas** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Replaced the two columns with one `member_id` column.\n\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n  - New `memberId(...)` helper builds `REGION + FY + HASH8 + CHK`: region from postcode, 2-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registration date, the same SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) first-8-hex, and a Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n  - Collision handling (`deduplicatedMemberId`) now applies to the memberId.\n  - Removed the old `customerCode`/`deduplicatedCustomerCode`/`membershipNumber` helpers.\n  - `primaryIdentifier` now returns the memberId; the human audit line and the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event now carry `memberId`.\n\n- **`mapper/OwnerLocality.java`** \u2014 `regionFromMemberId`/`timezoneFromMemberId` derive the region as the leading letter run of the memberId (before the FY digits).\n\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `locality`/`timezone` now read from the memberId; removed the `checkDigit` mapping. (`memberId` auto-maps by name.)\n\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`; added `memberId` (drives DTO generation); updated the `locality` description.\n\nThe owner segment already references the memberId indirectly (its AREA derives from `locality`, now sourced from the memberId's region), and the fiscal-year value is now embedded in the memberId's FY segment.",
